ENT regime is the live evidence: a Fed that hiked on 16 Sep 2026 into headline PCE of 3.6% and core PCE of 3.1% is a Fed whose reaction function would not deliver a 50bp rally in a growth scare. With the possibility of multiple drawdowns I take 0.33. CONJUNCTION: assumed rho = +0.55, high and deliberate — both conjuncts are produced by the same inflationary/fiscal-dominant/term-premium regime, so they are far from independent. 0.30 x 0.33 = 0.099, lifted to ~0.18 for that correlation. Answer 18. Watch list: MOVE monthly averages, the 10y swaption-implied vol surface, Treasury primary-dealer net positions and SOFR-Treasury basis spreads as a proxy for basis-trade absorption capacity, DGS10 behaviour inside equity drawdown windows.","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:58.009Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"FRED DFII10 (10y TIPS real yield, daily, hard market data) records a monthly average below 1.60% for six consecutive months — against 2.60% observed on 30 Oct 2026.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2029\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Directly falsifies my core claim that real yields do not mean-revert downward. CQ4 P50 down from 1.95% to about 1.30% and P90 down ~60bp; CQ6-D up by roughly +8 and CQ6-C down by a similar amount; CQ3 P50 down ~0.2pp via the weaker-demand channel that would have produced the rally.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"The US REAL curve flattens to inversion: DFII30 minus DFII10 at or below 0bp on a 3-month average, against roughly +45bp observed (3.07% vs 2.62% on 2 Nov 2026).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies my variance attribution specifically — it would say the level is being driven by expected short rates (r*) rather than by duration absorption. Shifts ~30 points of my CQ4 variance budget from the term-premium/repression pair back to r*, cuts CQ4 P90 by ~50bp whil